A||||6||GT Bastard||How much should I mill the heads?||||1||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||05-23-2000||07:33 PM||||Anybody have recommendations on how much I should have my heads milled? I just don't want to mill them to the point of having to modify the manifold.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||05-23-2000||10:52 PM||||Just have the shop mill them enough to straighten it up. Shouldn't be more than a few thousands. Up to 0.010" is no problem, more than that, you may have to mill the intake side of the head too, in order for the intake manifold to fit right.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fastonpumpgas||05-23-2000||10:59 PM||||I milled .010 off my deck and and the head deck surface and ended up will .017 of head to piston clearance at TDC, there was still around .015 till the intake wouldnt seal..  So I would worry more about compression ratios and bending vavles or hitting the head||||reg||1
Z||000003||80's BOY||05-24-2000||12:10 PM||||have to agree...0.010 will be a good medium. that's what i had done to mine, also.||||reg||14
Z||000004||GT Bastard||05-27-2000||01:42 AM||||Shite!  My dad went ahead and milled them .020<P>Apparently the machinist and the pontiac rep told him this would be fine and he agreed.  Am I going to need to modify the intake manifold another portion of the head?  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||05-27-2000||02:12 AM||||<BR>  The Chevy Power book says that head milling should be limited to .030" due<BR>to the thinning of the deck near the water jackets. They recommend that<BR>milling *really* be limited to only what is necessary to flatten the head.<P>However, they specifically state that .030" is acceptable. Keep in mind that<BR>this limit is for hi-performance applications which are rarely seen on the<BR>street. A real 250HP, not the bolt-on HP addition.<P>Your .020" is fine and the machinist and dad was right. It will be fine.<P>Beyond .030" the intake must be milled to match the ports since they are now<BR>lower. Also, as you mill, the intake drops until it sits on the block and<BR>there is no gap for RTV to seal the ends.<P>If it makes you feel better, a friend and I have milled the heads .060"<BR>(DON'T DO IT) and mill matched the intake. The sealing bead at the ends are<BR>thin, but so far (30k miles), it's fine.<P>Terry<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||05-27-2000||02:43 PM||||Cool Terry, thanks for the assurance.... I'm a little high strung when it comes to my baby.  ||||reg||7
